Paragraphs 

.block of text enclosed within the <p> tag 
.helps divide content into manageable, readable, sections 
    .its go-to element for wrapping text in a web page that is meant to be displayed as a distinct paragraph


Properties
.the browser reduces multiple spaces added by users to a single space
.if a user adds various lines, the browser compresses them into one line
.by default, the display of the paragraph element is set to 'block', meaning each new paragraph is placed on a new line

<br> - element creates a line break, giving you a new line without starting a new paragraph
      . use it when I want to move to the next line without beginning a whole new paragraph 

<p> - supports the alignment attribute and allows us to align our paragraphs in left, right, or center alignment
    
    
Pointers
.avoiding nested paragraphs - each <p> tag should contain only the text for one block of content
.avoid using <p> for non-textual content - use appropriate tags for images, lists, etc., instead of wrapping them 
    in <p> tags

